module gunbc.rung_drop.let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, Enumerated, ReplacementStaged }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }

// THE DECLARED RUNG DROP for the emitter's failure to annotate a let-bound closure's parameters with
// their declared formal types, so the emitted Rust does not compile without an expected-type context.
// Authored 2026-11-27 by fierce-lark-359 (planning slice) on warm-fox-517's ruling, approved as its
// own plan-only slice by neat-badger-614. No operator escalation was made for this row; no
// gunbc.design_ruling entry is claimed by this row and no operator words exist to record.
//
// WHAT THE DROP CARRIES. The repair of roadmap row emission-ownership-facts-survive-lowering requires
// the five arms of emission-building-block-realization to reach their declared output for the
// let-bound-closure subject family. Those five arms are acc_local_closure,
// acc_local_closure_identity_only, acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step,
// acc_local_closure_escaping_closure and acc_local_closure_copies_context. Each produces an instrument
// subject whose emitter output is a let-bound Rust closure, and the emitter writes those closures
// WITHOUT parameter type annotations, producing E0282 at compile time. This drop covers the emission
// half of those five arms: the emitter's obligation to annotate parameters from the subject's declared
// formal types at the binding site.
//
// WHAT THIS DROP DOES NOT COVER. It does not cover the fold-step lambda path, which emits WITH
// parameter types: emit_rust_fold_method_call calls emit_typed_fold_lambda with resolved fallback_types
// derived from the fold's accumulator and element types (positive control, measured 2026-11-27 on
// origin/main: 539 occurrences of |acc: <RealType> across 60 seed files, all compiling with no
// expected-type context at those sites). It does not cover the instrument's semantic correctness, the
// subject's DAG declaration, or the claim execution. It does not cover lambda_param_type_strs, which
// correctly renders inferred types when they ARE resolved; the failure is that emit_typed_let passes
// vec!["_"] as fallback_types to lambda_param_type_strs, giving inference no type to work with, and
// when inference yields None the fallback "_" is emitted verbatim as the parameter annotation via
// apply_type_template2 with the Rust template "{0}: {1}". It does not cover hand-written Rust in the
// emitted file (seed Rust is outside every worker's authority on this lane).
//
// WHY PREVIOUS IS MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE. The emitter's structural path mechanically resolves and
// writes formal parameter types where wired: emit_typed_fold_lambda receives lambda_acc_type_str and
// fold_elem_type_str from emit_rust_fold_method_call, constructs fallback_types, and lambda_param_type_strs
// writes the resolved InferredNode type through apply_type_template2. Positive control: 539 sites on
// origin/main, executing, compiling, with no expected-type context needed at the emitted closure. The
// mechanism is present and mechanically prevents untyped parameters wherever it fires. The five
// let-bound subjects fall off that mechanical path: emit_typed_let passes a hardcoded vec!["_"] as
// fallback_types instead of resolving from the subject's declared param_node type expressions, so the
// mechanism that the fold path executes is not wired to their binding site. The rung is the minimum
// across the class's in-scope paths: where the mechanism is wired it holds MechanicallyPreventable;
// where it is not (the let-binding path), the population sits below it.
//
// WHY TEMPORARY IS MITIGATABLE. For the five let-bound subjects, the emitter produces bad output
// unconditionally: the parameter annotation is always "_", never a resolved type. No mechanical check
// inside the emitter prevents this: emit_typed_let passes vec!["_"] and lambda_param_type_strs emits it
// verbatim. The E0282 at the emit-compile leg is a downstream consumer (rustc) catching bad emitter
// output, not the emitter preventing it. The worker's action is observation and reporting: name the
// hole at the leg where it fires and carry it, not attempt a fix in seed Rust (which is outside every
// worker's authority on this lane). This matches the precedent crate_row_names_a_module_the_emitter_has_no_reason_to_write:
// its 13 modules also never had the rung (no authored reference gave the emitter a reason to write
// their bodies), and the drop carries them at Mitigatable because the available action is reporting,
// not prevention.
//
// MEASURED BASIS, all counts printed on origin/main 2026-11-27, no slot spent. The untyped emitted
// marker |param: _| appears 3 times in seed Rust (v1_compiler_infer.rs:30944, :30981, :31008 — each a
// fold lambda whose element param fell back to _ because collection_element_type was unresolved; the
// same fallback mechanism that the let-binding path uses unconditionally). The typed marker
// |acc: <RealType> appears 539 times across 60 files in src/, confirming the fold path does emit typed
// parameters correctly. The asymmetry is structural: emit_typed_let hardcodes elem_type_str to
// "_".to_string(), while emit_rust_fold_method_call derives lambda_acc_type_str and fold_elem_type_str
// from the fold call's resolved types. tidy-hawk-691's acquisition on srv1 (slot 9,
// 2026-11-27T14:22:15Z, BOOT c095c0cd, head 435289c1c1129dbb3add4d4d12cc3063b20c84a0) produced
// 3 E0282 errors and 5 total errors, first at subjects.rs:138:60 at the acc_local_closure scale binding.
data let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "the emitter's obligation to annotate a let-bound closure's parameters from the subject's declared formal types at the binding site, carried for the repair of emission-ownership-facts-survive-lowering and the five let-bound-closure arms of emission-building-block-realization: acc_local_closure, acc_local_closure_identity_only, acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step, acc_local_closure_escaping_closure and acc_local_closure_copies_context",

  declared: "2026-11-27",

  standing: Standing { declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: ReplacementStaged { replacement: "the emitter resolves each let-bound closure's declared formal parameter types at the binding site and passes them as fallback_types to lambda_param_type_strs, in place of the hardcoded vec![\"_\"] that emit_typed_let passes today, so the emitted Rust compiles with no expected-type context" },
    population: Enumerated { members: FreeSemigroup { head: "acc_local_closure", tail: ["acc_local_closure_identity_only", "acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step", "acc_local_closure_escaping_closure", "acc_local_closure_copies_context"] } },
    restoration_trigger: "THE EMITTER ANNOTATES A LET-BOUND CLOSURE'S PARAMETERS FROM THE SUBJECT'S DECLARED FORMAL TYPES AT THE BINDING SITE, so the emitted Rust compiles with no expected-type context. Specifically: emit_typed_let resolves the param_node type expressions from the subject's formal declaration and passes them as the fallback_types Vec to lambda_param_type_strs, replacing the hardcoded vec![\"_\".to_string()] it passes today. Two things do NOT retire this drop: (1) rerunning the same instrument unchanged, which reproduces the same E0282 at the emit-compile leg; and (2) hand-writing Rust parameter annotations in the emitted file, which is seed Rust and is outside every worker's authority on this lane. A default or timed-out closure of any ask is not a ruling. No operator words exist for this row; none were sought.",
  } }
}
